	'k35e69d43' => 'Season ticket',
	'k36217d4a' => 'Opening on 30 October, Winter Ferry follows two strangers who find themselves thrown together on the deck of the last evening crossing across a freezing sound. As fog closes in and mechanical trouble delays their arrival, conversations uncover why neither traveler can easily return home. Designed by Rafael Duarte and featuring our resident acting ensemble, the staging uses timber decking and cold atmospheric haze to recreate the exposed vessel. Running time is two hours and ten minutes including one twenty-minute interval. Suitable for ages twelve and up. Previews take place on 30 and 31 October. Season ticket holders retain their chosen seats throughout the four-week run.',
	'k370c64d2' => 'Up to 48 hours before curtain.',
	'k37402773' => 'A standard season ticket for all five plays costs one hundred and ninety euros, representing substantial savings compared to buying single performances. For theatergoers aged twenty-five and under, our under-26 season ticket is available for ninety-five euros. To spread the cost across the year, subscribers may choose to pay in two equal instalments, with the first payment due upon booking in June and the second balance collected in December. For single visits, regular performance tickets cost forty-eight euros, preview performances cost thirty-two euros, and under-26 single tickets cost twenty-four euros. Backstage tours on Saturdays cost twelve euros.',
