	'k436b8169' => 'The season concludes with Salt and Thunder, opening on 23 April and running through 16 May. When a devastating gale strikes a small harbor town, the surviving community convenes an improvised maritime trial to determine accountability for a wrecked trawler. Staged under hard sidelight with live atmospheric sound, this intense ensemble piece questions duty, neighborly solidarity, and the burdens of survival. Running time is two hours and twenty minutes including one interval, suitable for ages fourteen and up. Previews run on 23 and 24 April. The final performance on 16 May closes our 2026–27 season.',
