	'k50b2c15a' => 'Butai Playhouse was established in 2009 by theatre director Tomas Reyes and producer Margit Ellison. Taking over a derelict municipal tram depot at 14 Lantern Row, they envisioned a theatre that would strip away commercial distractions and refocus attention entirely on the actor and the text. The word butai means stage, reflecting our core commitment to the physical playing space. From our earliest performances, the playhouse has committed to presenting five plays each season with a resident company of actors, allowing our community to experience a sustained conversation across varied works each year.',
