	'ka5a74947' => 'Our midwinter production is A House with Nine Doors, an energetic domestic comedy opening on 15 January. When an eccentric family gathers on Lantern Row to prepare their ancestral estate for sale, long-buried squabbles erupt across a labyrinth of adjoining rooms and misplaced keys. The piece tests the comic timing of eight ensemble actors navigating nine practical doorways on our end-on stage. Running time is two hours including an interval, with age guidance of ten and older. Previews run on 15 and 16 January. Performances run Tuesday through Saturday at 19:30 with Sunday matinees at 15:00.',
	'ka6707003' => 'Season tickets explained',
