	'kaa56b09a' => 'From Tram Depot to Repertory Theatre',
	'kaab03f13' => 'Can I choose my exact seat online or by phone?',
	'kab752578' => 'rows to the furthest seat',
	'kad356485' => '→ Now playing: The Lamp Room',
	'kad6c2776' => 'hello@butai-playhouse.example. Press tickets are held for opening nights; ask at least ten days ahead.',
	'kad8e6cec' => 'Ask about groups',
	'kadce7fed' => 'Book one performance',
	'kade06e1b' => 'The Auditorium Layout and Accessible Spaces',
	'kae6fdd80' => 'Any seat, stalls or circle, one price. Previews €32, under-26 €24.',
	'kaebfe467' => 'House',
	'kaedc194c' => 'THE 2026–27 SEASON — FIVE PLAYS —',
	'kaf79cf73' => 'Play three',
	'kb03036c4' => 'The Understudy',
	'kb0321c37' => 'Play two · opens 30 Oct',
	'kb0607689' => 'Milestones in Our Playhouse History',
	'kb06d7965' => '10% at the bar',
	'kb0abf70c' => 'Play three · opens 15 Jan',
	'kb0b58c58' => 'Every season ticket holder keeps the same seat across all five productions. There are no price tiers or sightline compromises in our auditorium; every row is steeply raked and no seat sits more than eleven rows from the stage.',
	'kb2872e0d' => 'Key Season Dates and Booking Milestones',
	'kb29f82b4' => 'Seats',
	'kb2aeeb5b' => 'Seven permanent staff lead Butai Playhouse alongside a resident company of eight actors who join us for the full September to May run. They work across rehearsals, scenic construction and wings coordination, and most of them can be found at the stage door by five o’clock.',
	'kb3da7939' => 'The brick building at 14 Lantern Row was originally constructed in the early twentieth century as a municipal tram depot for Easthaven. Following decades of industrial use, the structure stood dormant until 2009, when artistic director Tomas Reyes and executive director Margit Ellison undertook its careful conversion into an independent repertory playhouse. Rather than masking the building\'s industrial origins, the renovation preserved the exposed brickwork, steel roof trusses, and lofty timber ceilings. Today, the venue provides a permanent home for five annual productions, housing our stage, administrative offices, and rehearsal rooms under one roof.',
	'kb4bd16a9' => 'Under-26 season',
	'kb51a9926' => 'Tuesday to Saturday 12:00–18:00, and until curtain on performance days.<br>Curtain 19:30, Sunday 15:00.',
	'kb62f1e8a' => 'Five plays',
	'kb973569d' => 'Contact the box office',
	'kb9ece18c' => 'T',
	'kba286686' => 'The stage · 19:29',
	'kbba3b7c8' => 'One free date swap per play',
	'kbbaff128' => 'Contact',
	'kbd18548b' => 'Play two · 30 OCT – 22 NOV',
	'kbdbc4dc4' => 'A season ticket reserves your preferred seat across all five productions in our 2026–27 repertory calendar. Subscribers receive their chosen seat for every run, ticket flexibility, and priority booking each spring.',
	'kbdd52160' => 'When booking accessible seating or organizing group visits of up to eight people, our team handles arrangements directly to confirm suitable accommodation. If you require one of our four wheelchair positions in row J, companion seating, or access to the induction hearing loop, specify these details on your request form. Box office manager Jonas Berg coordinates all accessibility allocations before releasing surrounding seats. For assistance with step-free arrival or advice on specific rows, call +44 1632 960 527 from Tuesday to Saturday between 12:00 and 18:00, or visit our timber counter at 14 Lantern Row.',
	'kbf4a420b' => 'Winter Ferry',
	'kbf733d8a' => 'Access',
	'kbfc64282' => 'The season',
	'kc1c694bd' => 'Tickets',
	'kc21ebe10' => 'Priority renewals for existing season subscribers begin on 4 May and run through 31 May. On 1 June, season tickets go on general sale at one hundred and ninety euros for all five productions. Single performance tickets become available on 3 August at forty-eight euros, with under-26 tickets priced at twenty-four euros. The season officially opens on 18 September with The Lamp Room and concludes on 16 May after Salt and Thunder finishes its run. All evening performances begin promptly at 19:30 from Tuesday to Saturday, with Sunday matinees scheduled for 15:00.',
	'kc22b201f' => 'Play one · 18 SEPT – 11 OCT',
	'kc26e9d99' => 'Joining our mailing list is entirely free and requires only an email address. You will receive exactly one email per month, sent on the first Monday morning. We never sell, rent, or share your contact details with external organizations, sponsors, or advertising networks. If you ever wish to cancel your subscription, every issue includes a direct one-click unsubscribe link at the foot of the message, or you may email hello@butai-playhouse.example with your request. We handle your email address with the same quiet care we bring to our theatre.',
	'kc272c73f' => '9.5 m',
	'kc2825f49' => 'Saturdays at 11:00, about an hour',
	'kc2c347f5' => 'The playhouse is easily reached using public transport. Tram line 4 stops at Lantern Row, leaving visitors just a three-minute walk from our entrance. For those arriving by regional rail, Easthaven Central station is a twelve-minute walk through the neighborhood. Please note that Butai Playhouse does not operate a venue parking facility, and on-street parking in surrounding residential streets is restricted. Visitors traveling by bicycle are welcome to use the sheltered bicycle racks located beside our side stage door. We advise allowing ample time to arrive, collect tickets, and enjoy a drink before beginners are called.',
	'kc5f29bb3' => 'Privacy',
	'kc6bce625' => '— From the rehearsal room',
	'kc7e2158b' => 'The Rehearsal Room, Workshop, and Saturday Tours',
	'kc8016bb1' => 'Lights, rigs and checks the stage each afternoon.',
	'kceb91e1c' => 'Play one',
	'kcede7e98' => 'An Intimate Two-Hundred-Seat Auditorium',
	'kd0056397' => 'Season ticket renewals run from 4 to 31 May, before general season tickets go on sale on 1 June, and single tickets follow on 3 August. Our five openings then arrive one by one, and the season closes on 16 May.',
	'kd08e9513' => '→ Plan your visit',
	'kd0a7cb8d' => 'The same seat every time',
	'kd2960f92' => 'Box office (Sunday)',
	'kd2b605d7' => 'Tomas Reyes',
	'kd33b960c' => 'Booking your place at Butai Playhouse follows four straightforward steps. First, choose whether you are securing a full five-play season ticket or reserving tickets for a single performance. Second, consult our house plan to select your preferred seats; whether you book online, telephone our box office, or visit in person, our staff refer to the exact same layout. Third, complete your payment, after which we will promptly email a booking confirmation displaying your designated row and seat numbers. Fourth, your seat remains yours; simply collect your printed ticket at the box office or present your confirmation email upon arrival.',
	'kd4b9aa05' => 'Housed in a former municipal tram depot converted in 2009, Butai Playhouse brings audiences face to face with live performance. The building brings together an intimate auditorium, rehearsal space, and an active carpentry workshop.',
	'kd4c3d738' => 'On-sale dates',
	'kd507a77f' => '2 · Pick your seat',
	'kd9d25764' => 'Ask the box office',
	'kdaa1f07c' => 'Tuesday to Saturday; on performance days until curtain',
	'kdc4531a0' => 'Opening on 5 March, The Understudy takes audiences into the claustrophobic tension of backstage life. Set in the half-hour before curtain call, the drama centers on an understudy who suddenly learns they must step onto the stage after months of silent waiting in the wings. Directed by Tomas Reyes with lighting design by Lena Vogt, the play captures the terror and discipline of professional repertory performance. Running time is one hour and fifty minutes with no interval. Recommended for audiences aged fourteen and over. Previews take place on 5 and 6 March.',
	'kdcc7593f' => '→ Now playing',
	'kdccd8cd6' => 'The wings · 19:29',
	'kdce6b84e' => 'We do not charge different prices for different rows in our two-hundred-seat house. Whether you choose front stalls or circle, tickets are priced simply, and a season ticket can be paid in two equal instalments in June and December.',
	'kdd753679' => 'I',
	'kdd7bf230' => 'Address',
	'kddaf5ccc' => 'How does the seat request process work for groups and accessibility?',
	'kde8b1c6d' => 'We are committed to making our productions welcoming and accessible to all patrons. The ground-floor stalls provide step-free access throughout, including four designated wheelchair spaces located in row J. Our auditorium is equipped with an induction hearing loop that functions across all performances. Additionally, the second Thursday performance of each four-week run features open captioning displayed on screens beside the stage. An attended cloakroom is available in the foyer free of charge for coats and umbrellas, and our foyer bar serves drinks and refreshments before the show and during the interval.',
	'kde8e41a2' => 'The 2026–27 season opens on 18 September with The Lamp Room, a new play that chronicles a veteran lighthouse keeper facing his final winter on an isolated coastal station. Directed by Tomas Reyes, the production explores solitude, memory, and the routine of tending an oil lantern against encroaching darkness. The play runs for one hour and forty-five minutes without an interval and is recommended for audiences aged fourteen and older. The first two performances on 18 and 19 September are previews, offering early access before official opening night. Single tickets cost forty-eight euros, while preview seats are thirty-two euros. Every seat in the house shares the same price.',
	'kdec48c1e' => 'Email the box office',
	'ke09796d9' => 'SINCE 2009 — SINCE 2009 —',
	'ke101bb9d' => 'For assistance with ticket purchases, season subscriptions, seat requests, or date exchanges, contact box office manager Jonas Berg. Our counter at 14 Lantern Row is open Tuesday through Saturday from 12:00 to 18:00, and on Sundays from 13:30 to 15:00 when matinees are scheduled. You may telephone us directly during opening hours on +44 1632 960 527, or write by email to boxoffice@butai-playhouse.example. All seat booking requests and date swap inquiries submitted online or by email are processed within one working day in the order received.',
	'ke16dd6e1' => 'Prices',
	'ke2b842b0' => 'Data Security, Rights, and Contact Information',
	'ke3544a20' => 'One company',
	'ke43fd40f' => 'Single tickets on sale',
	'ke4c57054' => 'The Lamp Room',
	'ke5427573' => 'Our technical and visual standards are maintained by stage manager Imani Okafor, technical and lighting manager Lena Vogt, and resident designer Rafael Duarte. Imani Okafor oversees rehearsal schedules, prompt books, and cue-calling from the wings, maintaining discipline across all performance evenings. Lena Vogt manages theatre lighting, electrical safety, and technical stage machinery, conducting daily equipment checks at 16:00 before house doors open. Rafael Duarte designs costumes and physical environments for all five productions, working directly with our workshop carpenters to build sets scaled specifically to our 9.5-meter stage.',
	'ke5d9de39' => 'Five',
	'ke6a6af19' => 'How do renewals and priority booking work?',
	'ke6ddbf18' => 'Before the show',
	'ke6fd3e1f' => 'SEASON TICKETS — SEASON TICKETS —',
	'ke7021ade' => 'Play five · opens 23 Apr',
	'ke8e655c6' => 'Two hundred',
	'ke908b461' => 'Five plays, the same seat every time. Pay in two instalments, June and December.',
	'kea1e9ff3' => 'A Butai Playhouse season ticket covers admission to all five productions in our 2026–27 season: The Lamp Room, Winter Ferry, A House with Nine Doors, The Understudy, and Salt and Thunder. Your subscription secures the exact same seat in our two-hundred-seat auditorium for every opening run. If your schedule changes, you are entitled to one free date swap per play, provided you notify the box office at least forty-eight hours before curtain. In addition, season subscribers receive a complimentary copy of our bound season programme book, a ten percent discount at the playhouse bar, and priority renewal rights each May.',
	'keab87b1f' => 'Seven plus eight',
	'keaed4fb3' => 'Jonas Berg',
	'keb4335b6' => 'Plays',
	'keb6ca629' => 'Built 2009',
	'kec4987a2' => 'Open the seat plan',
	'ked210d45' => 'When you purchase a season ticket, reserve seats for a single performance, or submit a seat request form through our website, we collect your name, email address, telephone number, and seat preferences. This information is used strictly to process your booking, issue confirmation emails, allocate seats on our house plan, and notify you in the rare event of a performance schedule change. We do not store payment card numbers on our local servers. Ticket records are retained to honor date swaps and facilitate priority subscription renewals each spring.',
	'kef0a75b7' => 'Executive director and co-founder',
	'kef0bb29c' => 'Aisha Rahman',
	'kef8c1fbc' => 'Resident designer',
	'kefc56b3d' => 'The Understudy opens',
	'kf27279a0' => 'Programmes all five plays and directs one a season.',
	'kf2cc81f2' => 'Accessibility, Captioned Shows, and Facilities',
	'kf38ef96c' => 'Yes. You can specify your preferred row and seat numbers when placing a request through this website, calling our box office team, or stopping by Lantern Row. Because every seat in the house is sold at one uniform price, you never pay a premium for front stalls or front circle locations. If submitting our online seat request form, note your desired seating area, the performance title, and the date. Our box office team processes submissions within one working day and replies with confirmed seat allocations and a direct payment link. You can also email boxoffice@butai-playhouse.example.',
	'kf3e3e2e1' => 'Imani Okafor',
	'kf3f2a026' => 'Season 26/27',
	'kf62e456f' => 'Costumes and sets, built in our own workshop.',
	'kf65d6e23' => 'Our artistic philosophy rests on three unchanging principles. First, we operate as a genuine repertory company, keeping one company of eight actors together for nine months to rehearse by day and perform by night. Second, every seat in our house is sold for the exact same price: forty-eight euros for single tickets or one hundred and ninety euros for the season, ensuring that physical access to art is never stratified by income. Third, we produce theatre without pretense or amplification, relying on architectural intimacy, skilled lighting, and truthful stagecraft.',
	'kf78246f1' => 'Rehearsal Notes and Early Ticket Notices',
	'kf7e7cbb9' => '30 Oct',
	'kf8a6df2c' => 'The rehearsal room',
	'kf9c2bf9f' => 'Request seats',
	'kfb0632a9' => 'What The Call Sheet Delivers Each Month',
	'kfb8c45cf' => 'Preview performance',
	'kfe08d5af' => 'Co-founders Tomas Reyes and Margit Ellison have guided Butai Playhouse since its opening in 2009. As artistic director, Tomas Reyes selects the five plays comprising each season and directs several of the annual productions, emphasizing tight ensemble work and direct storytelling. Executive director Margit Ellison manages the theatre\'s operational sustainability, season subscriptions, and long-term planning, ensuring the playhouse maintains its financial independence without relying on speculative commercial ventures. Together, they established the theatre\'s defining policy that every seat across the auditorium should be available at one accessible, uniform price.',
	'kfe1221d6' => '→ Choose your seat',
	'kff0e0377' => 'To preserve the concentration of the actors and the experience of fellow audience members in our intimate auditorium, auditorium doors close promptly at curtain time. Patrons arriving after 19:30 for evening shows or 15:00 for Sunday matinees will be asked to wait in the foyer bar. Front of house staff will admit latecomers only during a suitable break in the performance, which is determined in advance by stage manager Imani Okafor and director Tomas Reyes. In certain productions with continuous action or no interval, late admission may not be possible until the intermission.',
	'kff1c0f5d' => 'One price, any seat. Tell us the play, the date and how many seats; we reply within one working day with seat numbers and a payment link.',
	'kffb7e666' => 'Newsletter',
	'search_results' => 'Search results for: %s',
);
